    "registration": {
      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "WEI Hsi 魏禧 (T. 氷[凝]叔, H. 勺庭, 叔子 and 裕齋) Mar. 2, 1624–1681, c. Jan. 6, scholar, a native of Ning-tu, Kiangsi, was the son of a philanthropist, Wei Chao-fêng 魏兆鳳 (T. 聖期, 1596–1654). In his youth Wei Hsi was greatly influenced by the scholarship of his sister's husband, Ch'iu Wei-p'ing 邱維屏 (T. 邦士, H. 松下先生, 1614–1679).",
          "source": "eccp-3674951",
          "kind": "source-wording",
          "status": "imported"
        },
        {
          "text": "魏禧，字冰叔，寧都人。",
